---
title: State diagram - user account (User.IsActive, User.EmailConfirmed; origin/main, 499c39d)
---
stateDiagram-v2
    direction LR

    state "Registered, unconfirmed<br>IsActive = true<br>EmailConfirmed = false<br>(cannot sign in)" as Unconfirmed
    state "Active<br>IsActive = true<br>EmailConfirmed = true<br>(can sign in)" as Active
    state "Inactive<br>IsActive = false<br>(cannot sign in or refresh)" as Inactive

    [*] --> Unconfirmed : register (policy checked)
    [*] --> Active : seeded
    Unconfirmed --> Active : confirm (NOT IMPLEMENTED)
    Active --> Inactive : suspend or soft delete
    Inactive --> Active : reinstate
    Active --> Active : reset password
    Inactive --> Inactive : reset password
    Unconfirmed --> Unconfirmed : reset password

    note right of Inactive
        Suspend and soft delete both only set IsActive = false,
        so they are one stored state and reinstate undoes either.
        Repeating suspend, delete or reinstate returns 409.
        Reset password (single-use 30-minute token + policy)
        changes only the hash and revokes refresh tokens:
        IsActive and EmailConfirmed are not checked or changed.
        No lockout state, only the per-IP rate limit (429).
    end note
